Q.4 Data Warehouse\
\
Which requirement is the strongest fit for a data warehouse?\
\
d.  Run controlled business reporting over trusted structured data\
\
\
\
Q.5  schema on Read or schema on write\
\
A. Data is stored first and interpreted when it is read \'97 schema on read\
B. Data must match an expected structure before it is accepted into the target. \'97 schema on write\
C. A raw JSON area keeps different optional fields. \'97\'97\'97 schema on read\
D. A controlled reporting table requires known columns and types. \'97 \'97 schema on write\
\
\
\
Q.6 Design bronze and silver rules\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs32 \cf2 \cb6 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Bronze \'97 keep everything. Bronze is the raw, immutable landing layer: all rows, all columns, exactly as received. No cleaning, no filtering, no transformation \'97 only technical ingestion metadata (
\f2\fs28 ingest_timestamp
\f1\fs32 , 
\f2\fs28 source_file
\f1\fs32 , 
\f2\fs28 batch_id
\f1\fs32 ) is added. Duplicates, nulls, bad types and out-of-range values are all preserved, because Bronze must be a faithful, replayable record of what the source sent.\
Silver \'97 check and clean. Silver applies data-quality rules: cast types (
\f2\fs28 amount_gbp \uc0\u8594  DECIMAL
\f1\fs32 ), enforce non-null on 
\f2\fs28 order_id
\f1\fs32  and 
\f2\fs28 amount_gbp
\f1\fs32 , validate ranges (
\f2\fs28 amount_gbp >= 0
\f1\fs32 ), standardise 
\f2\fs28 city
\f1\fs32  and 
\f2\fs28 status
\f1\fs32  against controlled vocabularies, deduplicate to one row per 
\f2\fs28 order_id
\f1\fs32 , and quarantine invalid rows into a 
\f2\fs28 silver_rejected
\f1\fs32  table with a 
\f2\fs28 reject_reason
\f1\fs32  \'97 never silently drop them. The result is trusted, typed, conformed row-level data ready for Gold (star schema / 
\f2\fs28 FactSales
\f1\fs32 ).\
\
Q. 8 silver\
\
Which record belongs most naturally in silver?\
\
C. A cleaned and deduplicated order row\
\
