Q.13 compute or storage\
\
A. Files kept for later use \'97 storage\
B. CPU and memory used to run a transformation \'97 Compute\
C. Stored analytical table data \'97 storage\
D. Processing resources used for a query \'97 compute\
\
Q.14 why separate compute and storage?\
\
\cb1 they scale differently, cost differently, and fail differently \'97 so coupling them forces you to pay for the worst case of both.\
